<section image-layout="blank" id="3qt0QpLHtM" background-color="heading"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="1opVfQguwm" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">The Invisible Shield Club</p><h1 font-size="44pt">The sky has an invisible shield</h1><p font-size="lg">Sunlight brings light and warmth. High above the weather, ozone absorbs much of the Sun’s harmful ultraviolet, or UV. Join the club: see the shield, test what it changes and learn how people protect it.</p><spacer size="20pt"></spacer><p font-size="sm">Source: <a href="https://www.unep.org/news-and-stories/press-release/ozone-layer-recovery-track-helping-avoid-global-warming-05degc">UNEP ozone assessment</a></p></grid-item><grid-item id="7v4WM39aqT" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/H0HMR0HoI1NmcAWHrHsyc.png" saved-media-id="r6l8a8p1w4xlhdg" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="atmosphere-cut-paper" alt="Layered cut-paper editorial science illustration of Earth curving across the lower right, cloud-white land beneath a thin shield-blue atmospheric arc, several UV-gold sunlight paths arriving from the upper left with some ending in the blue region and some continuing, deep-ink outer space, clean vector-like edges, subtle paper fibers, bright optimistic mood, no text or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="lqrsvuutJZ" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="eKBuCula7u"><h2>Meet ozone: three oxygen atoms</h2><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="Oxw9pR7csX" vertical-align="center" colspan="23"><p>Ozone is <b>O₃</b>: three oxygen atoms joined together. Most protective ozone floats in the <b>stratosphere</b>, the calm layer above our weather.</p><p>It is a region of gas, not a solid shell. Ozone near the ground is a separate pollution problem.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="swhEUOzs1b" vertical-align="center" colspan="37"><freeform-block w="560" h="300"><shape preset="line" x="78" y="108" w="70" h="2" stroke="palette-4" stroke-width="5"></shape><shape preset="line" x="158" y="108" w="70" h="2" stroke="palette-4" stroke-width="5"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="28" y="68" w="82" h="82" fill="accent" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="113" y="68" w="82" h="82" fill="accent" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="198" y="68" w="82" h="82" fill="accent" stroke-width="0"></shape><box type="content" x="34" y="92" w="70"><h3 align="center"><span text-color="#F8FCFF">O</span></h3></box><box type="content" x="119" y="92" w="70"><h3 align="center"><span text-color="#F8FCFF">O</span></h3></box><box type="content" x="204" y="92" w="70"><h3 align="center"><span text-color="#F8FCFF">O</span></h3></box><box type="content" x="65" y="166" w="180"><h3 align="center">O₃</h3><p align="center">one ozone molecule</p></box><box type="content" x="310" y="18" w="230" h="264" sizing="fixed" background-color="heading" style="border-radius: 18pt;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="325" y="78" w="200" h="58" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="padding: 8pt 12pt; border-radius: 12pt;"><p align="center"><b>Protective ozone region</b></p></box><shape preset="ellipse" x="334" y="207" w="182" h="62" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><box type="content" x="332" y="39" w="186"><p align="center"><span text-color="#F8FCFF"><b>Stratosphere</b></span></p></box><box type="content" x="347" y="181" w="156"><p align="center"><span text-color="#F8FCFF">weather below</span></p></box><box type="content" x="354" y="225" w="142"><p font-size="13pt" align="center"><b>Earth’s surface</b></p></box></freeform-block></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="RNiNDCAzSN"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="k1ar4jpiBP"><h2>Predict the UV path</h2><p>Imagine two identical Earths receiving the same harmful UV. One has more stratospheric ozone; one has less. Which ground receives less UV?</p><freeform-block w="840" h="286"><box type="content" w="405" h="278" sizing="fixed" background-color="heading" style="border-radius: 18pt;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="435" w="405" h="278" sizing="fixed" background-color="heading" style="border-radius: 18pt;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="24" y="16" w="180"><h3><span text-color="#F8FCFF">More ozone</span></h3></box><box type="content" x="459" y="16" w="180"><h3><span text-color="#F8FCFF">Less ozone</span></h3></box><shape preset="ellipse" x="35" y="62" w="54" h="54" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="470" y="62" w="54" h="54" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="line" x="132" y="73" w="2" h="102" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="184" y="73" w="2" h="102" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="236" y="73" w="2" h="102" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="567" y="73" w="2" h="102" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="619" y="73" w="2" h="102" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="671" y="73" w="2" h="102" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><box type="content" x="38" y="168" w="329" h="28" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="border-radius: 999pt;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="473" y="168" w="329" h="28" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="border-radius: 999pt;"><p></p></box><shape preset="ellipse" x="94" y="174" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="139" y="174" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="184" y="174" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="229" y="174" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="274" y="174" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="565" y="174" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="694" y="174" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="82" y="208" w="240" h="92" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="517" y="208" w="240" h="92" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><box type="content" x="116" y="224" w="172"><h3 align="center">?</h3><p font-size="13pt" align="center">UV at the ground</p></box><box type="content" x="551" y="224" w="172"><h3 align="center">?</h3><p font-size="13pt" align="center">UV at the ground</p></box></freeform-block><p font-size="lg"><b>Point, vote and explain your reason.</b></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="19308SiV8o"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="oBNwTaEGl_"><h2>Reveal: what the shield changes</h2><freeform-block w="840" h="286"><box type="content" w="405" h="278" sizing="fixed" background-color="heading" style="border-radius: 18pt;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="435" w="405" h="278" sizing="fixed" background-color="heading" style="border-radius: 18pt;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="24" y="14" w="230"><h3><span text-color="#F8FCFF">More ozone</span></h3></box><box type="content" x="459" y="14" w="230"><h3><span text-color="#F8FCFF">Less ozone</span></h3></box><shape preset="ellipse" x="35" y="58" w="50" h="50" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="470" y="58" w="50" h="50" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="line" x="132" y="68" w="2" h="104" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="184" y="68" w="2" h="104" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="236" y="68" w="2" h="104" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="567" y="68" w="2" h="104" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="619" y="68" w="2" h="104" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="671" y="68" w="2" h="104" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><box type="content" x="38" y="166" w="329" h="28" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="border-radius: 999pt;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="473" y="166" w="329" h="28" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="border-radius: 999pt;"><p></p></box><shape preset="ellipse" x="126" y="172" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="178" y="172" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="230" y="172" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="561" y="172" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="613" y="172" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="665" y="172" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="line" x="236" y="194" w="2" h="45" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="619" y="194" w="2" h="45" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="671" y="194" w="2" h="45" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="82" y="214" w="240" h="92" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="517" y="214" w="240" h="92" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><box type="content" x="102" y="226" w="200"><h4 align="center">More is absorbed</h4><p font-size="13pt" align="center">Less harmful UV reaches the ground.</p></box><box type="content" x="537" y="226" w="200"><h4 align="center">Less is absorbed</h4><p font-size="13pt" align="center">More harmful UV can pass through.</p></box></freeform-block><p font-size="lg"><b>The shield changes the amount. It does not block every ray.</b></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="HueUPtAF2t" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Zb8ZzNdkB7"><h2>How people thinned the shield</h2><p>Some long-lived human-made gases are called <b>ozone-depleting substances</b> because they can start a repeating chain high above Earth.</p><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="medium" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="s40yfpmXbp" colspan="15"><h4>Stay for years</h4><p>The chemicals remain in the air for a long time.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="R_twdHQgHu" colspan="15"><h4>Drift upward</h4><p>Some eventually reach the stratosphere.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="cn1iOPbLtE" colspan="15"><h4>Sunlight opens them</h4><p>UV breaks them apart and releases reactive atoms.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="2T7--63o9U" colspan="15"><h4>Repeat the damage</h4><p>Those atoms can destroy ozone molecules again and again.</p></grid-item></grid><aside variant="info"><p>The protective region became thinner. It was not a neat, visible hole.</p></aside><p font-size="sm">Source: <a href="https://ozone.unep.org/treaties/montreal-protocol">UNEP, Montreal Protocol</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="lRYk8do10V"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="jocRN2P1k7"><h2>The comeback has a clock</h2><p>If current policies stay in place, a 2023 UN-backed assessment projects a return to 1980 ozone levels at different times.</p><smart-layout variant="minimalTimeline" orientation="horizontal" cell-size="15"><smart-layout-item><h4>Around 2040 · Global</h4><p>Ozone levels across most of the world could return first.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Around 2045 · Arctic</h4><p>Recovery near the North Pole is projected a little later.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Around 2066 · Antarctic</h4><p>Recovery near the South Pole is expected to take longest.</p></smart-layout-item></smart-layout><aside variant="success"><p>These are projections, not guaranteed dates. Continuing the plan matters.</p></aside><p font-size="sm">Source: <a href="https://www.unep.org/news-and-stories/press-release/ozone-layer-recovery-track-helping-avoid-global-warming-05degc">UNEP, 2023 assessment</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="t4ZxBoTxf-" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="MfhNM8-B5r"><h2>Different actions do different jobs</h2><p><b>Sort each action by its real job.</b> Similar words do not always mean the same solution.</p><grid marker="icon" marker-size="large" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" marker-straddle="true" spacing="medium" padding-top="42pt"><grid-item id="OeEMAGGiTp" background-color="palette-3" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/VAhQqo6ksmhC5yYcXMN6.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="international agreement protecting atmosphere" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black rounded shape, resembling a dome, against a white background, conveying the concept of atmosphere that surrounds the earth.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>Ozone recovery</h3><p>Countries phase out ozone-depleting substances. Trained adults safely service old cooling equipment.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="11df_VJl8z" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/HqRnqTOMvbrtWfZHXPTo.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="sun hat shade and sunscreen" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Sun symbolized by a circular shape with rays extending outwards, embodies the concept of the sun, conveying warmth, light, and energy.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>Sun safety</h3><p>Shade, clothing and sunscreen protect skin from UV now.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="P9l2pcvFle" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/LPgDsa9S3qAKztkGcTZ7.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="thermometer beside cooling unit" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A bulb with a long stem, symbolizing the concept of temperature measurement.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>Climate</h3><p>HFCs do not deplete ozone, but many can warm the climate.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="sm">Source: <a href="https://www.unep.org/news-and-stories/press-release/ozone-layer-recovery-track-helping-avoid-global-warming-05degc">UNEP</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="5s82U58uaU" background-color="heading"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="XgYs3KvHvV" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">Teach it back</p><h1>Your 20-second shield story</h1><grid divider="sm palette-5" marker="number" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="inline" direction="vertical" spacing="none" style="--marker-inline-size: 30pt; --marker-gap: 12pt;"><grid-item id="McqTWVnuN3" padding="8pt 0"><h4>Where?</h4><p>In the stratosphere, above the weather.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="IjTi_vPBtC" padding="8pt 0"><h4>What does it do?</h4><p>It absorbs much harmful UV; some still passes.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Nv2ptvmcJG" padding="8pt 0"><h4>What thinned it?</h4><p>Long-lived human-made chemicals reduced ozone.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="m2TxOvpbiX" padding="8pt 0"><h4>What plan is helping?</h4><p>Countries are phasing those chemicals out together.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="lg"><b>Finish with one accurate action—and one mix-up to avoid.</b></p></grid-item><grid-item id="5xBM1D6WpK" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/U-xDlB-5f2pctyAXHy_52.png" saved-media-id="eg2qgh3t3r7vfnx" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="atmosphere-cut-paper" alt="Layered cut-paper editorial science illustration of a curious ten-year-old pointing toward an Earth cutaway at the lower right, the Earth in the same orientation as a curved cloud-white surface beneath a thin shield-blue atmospheric arc, UV-gold rays arriving from the upper left with some stopping in the arc and one continuing, a small action-green circle suggesting cooperation, deep-ink space, clean vector-like edges, subtle paper fibers, confident optimistic classroom tone, no text or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>